  "form": {
    "$comment": "SELECTED RESPONSE ONLY. Sean Reynolds, 2026-09-03, after reading FORM-A as a teacher: 'this is a mixed classroom assessment, not a TCAP-field-testable form' and 'all the questions on the assessment builder need to be TCAP-style multiple choice, maybe multiple select.' The four-tier ladder existed to keep a DBQ slot on a form; that slot is what made the form a mixed instructional packet rather than an assessment. Extended responses and DBQs are NOT deleted — they leave the assessment builder and become their own branded activity (tools/dbq_activity.py), which is what they always were. Within a tier conformance is EXACT and fails in either direction.",
    "surface": "assessment",
    "allowedItemTypes": [
      "mcq",
      "multiple-select"
    ],
    "dokCeilingRationale": "DOK-4 is structurally impossible in a selected-response item, so a selected-response form CANNOT assess it and must say so on the page rather than pretend. The ceiling is 3 and it is printed. Previously the ladder answered this by requiring an extended item; that answer is withdrawn.",
